Call the systems $A$ and $I$, with Hilbert spaces $\mathcal S_A$ and $\mathcal S_I$. Their composite space is $\mathcal S_{AI}=\mathcal S_A\otimes\mathcal S_I.$ Choose orthonormal bases $\{\ket{a}\}$ and $\{\ket{i}\}$ for the two factors. Pair every basis vector of the first system with every basis vector of the second: $\ket{a}\otimes\ket{i}\equiv\ket{a\,i}.$ If the factor spaces have dimensions $D_A$ and $D_I$, then $\dim\mathcal S_{AI}=D_A D_I.$ The inner product factorizes, $\braket{b\,j}{a\,i}
=\braket{b}{a}\braket{j}{i}
=\delta_{ba}\delta_{ji}.$ Thus two composite basis states are orthogonal whenever either subsystem label differs.

