Now take two spins. Denote the components of the first by $\sigma_x,\sigma_y,\sigma_z$, and those of the second by $\tau_x,\tau_y,\tau_z$. In a $z$-basis, the composite basis is $\ket{uu},\qquad \ket{ud},\qquad \ket{du},\qquad \ket{dd}.$ The first slot always refers to $\sigma$, the second to $\tau$. A general state is $\ket{\Psi}
=c_{uu}\ket{uu}+c_{ud}\ket{ud}
+c_{du}\ket{du}+c_{dd}\ket{dd}.$

